+ * performance cores (CPU sets); with several last-level caches (Ryzen CCDs)
+ * the frame and its workers stay in one big enough group; the game thread,
+ * the translation and the sound core get ideal processors on different cores,
+ * and with SMT and enough cores the workers stay off the game thread's and the
+ * translation's cores. Printed at start as "[sched] processors:" and
+ * "[sched] placement:" lines. PS3_SCHED_PLACE=0 = none of it (patch 0047's
+ * behaviour). The worker pools ask for their default size here:
+ * HS_ROLE_SPURS = jobs of a SPURS job list at once (the chain walker
+ * included), HS_ROLE_VERTEX = vertex-fetch workers; their own overrides
+ * (SPURS_JOB_THREADS, RSX_VERTEX_THREADS) still win. */
